          "description": "Mid-troposphere, step 601 level 41 (T = 265.53 K, M = 1.3856e19 molec/cm3). Half the surface air density and 43 K colder.\n\nReference: Vdot from cbmz_mosaic_Fun, the KPP-generated right-hand side, evaluated on the dumped var_in with the dumped RCONST by the real64 replay kernels/cbmz_driver (WRF's KPP is already real64, so this is an independent replay of the same arithmetic rather than a precision upgrade). This is the INSTANTANEOUS rate, which WRF never writes: over its 60 s step the finite increment (var_out - var_in)/60 reaches only 2.7e5 to 8.0e6 molec/cm3/s where Fun reaches 1.1e6 to 3.6e7, a factor of 4 to 35, so a tendency test referenced against differenced states would be testing something else entirely.\n\nShape: each d<SPC>_dt is an observed written D(CBMZ.<SPC>, t), which esm-spec 7.4 resolves to the tendency the reaction system already derives, so asserting it at time 0 evaluates the mechanism's right-hand side at the given state. The time_span is empty ({start: 0, end: 0}), the shape esm-spec 6.6.2 names for a document with ODE states all of whose assertions sit at t0: the runner answers from the initial state without integrating. This adds no physics -- it is the derivative-test surface of the mechanism, and it pins the whole stoichiometric matrix and every rate law at once, independently of any integrator. The peroxy coefficients are live here as everywhere in this document, but at t = 0 that is no different from WRF: the operator split of FORTRAN_BUGS N107 opens up only as the step proceeds.\n\nHCl and NH3 are absent from the 64: they are reservoir species of this mechanism (see their declarations), so no D(CBMZ.X, t) exists for them. What such an assertion would say -- that the CBM-Z gas phase produces and destroys neither -- is structural in this document rather than numerical.\n\nMeasured: 42 of the 64 assertions are BIT-IDENTICAL to KPP and the largest residual is 1.4e-12 (dOH_dt)\n\nState: data/eqwefic/dumps/chem170_wrf/esm_dump_cbmz_kpp_601.json level k = 41; reference chem170_scm/replay/kp_601.out.json (variable vdot). The run is described in data/eqwefic/notes/chem170_scm_reference_run.md.",
