        {
          "id": "rich_surface_terpenes_tendencies",
          "description": "The rich column's first chemistry call (step 1, 06 LST, surface). API 1.2e10 and LIM 4.7e9 molec/cm3, so reactions {137:117}..{142:122} carry flux here and nowhere else in either column -- alpha-pinene's lifetime against ozone at 30 ppb is under a quarter of a second, and limonene's under an eighth, so dAPI_dt and dLIM_dt are among the largest tendencies in the whole test suite. The aromatic and isoprene primaries are at their initial values too.\n\nWhich column this is. The reference is the RICH chem_opt = 170 column, dumps/chem170_rich -- a SECOND reference run, not a recapture of the first. Same sounding, location, dates, namelist and binary as the six idealized regimes; the only difference is ESM_RICH_IC=1, which raises seven initial mixing ratios that WRF-Chem's idealized gas profile leaves at its 1e-11 to 1e-13 ppb floor: TOL 0.50, XYL 0.30, CSL 0.01, ISO 2.00, API 0.50, LIM 0.20 and C2H5OH 1.00 ppb (chem/chemics_init.F, CBMZ_MOSAIC_KPP case, WRF fork branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170). dumps/chem170_wrf is untouched. Without it the aromatic, isoprene and terpene columns of the stoichiometric matrix are multiplied by concentrations of 1e-3 molec/cm3 and the test cannot tell a right coefficient from a wrong one; here those reactions carry flux. The two columns are not the same run at different times -- their meteorology diverges as well, through the aerosol path of FORTRAN_BUGS N86.\n\nNothing else changes: same Fun reference from kernels/cbmz_driver, same t = 0 evaluation on an empty time_span, same rel 1e-9. The frozen coefficients of N107 do not enter at t = 0.\n\nMeasured: 58 of the 64 assertions are BIT-IDENTICAL to KPP and the largest residual is 3.0e-16 (dH2O2_dt)\n\nState: data/eqwefic/dumps/chem170_rich/esm_dump_cbmz_kpp_1.json level k = 1; reference chem170_rich/replay/kp_1.out.json (variable vdot); run script data/eqwefic/chem170_rich/run.sh.",
