  "reaction_systems": {
    "CBMZ": {
      "reference": {
        "notes": "WRF v4.8.0 chem/KPP/mechanisms/cbmz_mosaic/cbmz_mosaic.eqn (142 reactions, of which the three identity rows 124-126 are omitted here as KPP itself omits them from Fun) and cbmz_mosaic.spc (66 variable + 2 fixed species). WRF species names are the KPP names unchanged apart from case (cbmz_mosaic_wrfkpp.equiv)."
      },
      "species": {
        "H2SO4": {
          "units": "molec/cm^3",
          "default": 167793844.05364805,
          "description": "CBM-Z species H2SO4 (KPP VAR index 1); default = the surface-noon state of the reference column."
        },
        "HCl": {
          "units": "molec/cm^3",
          "constant": true,
          "default": 6853211902.568538,
          "description": "HCl (KPP VAR index 2), a RESERVOIR species of this mechanism. It is a KPP VAR species, but its only appearance in cbmz_mosaic.eqn is the identity row {124:104} HCl = HCl, which has zero net stoichiometry and which KPP eliminates from Fun along with the reaction; the generated code writes Vdot = 0 for it and this document says the same thing with constant: true. HCl is in the mechanism because MOSAIC partitions it into the aerosol, not because the gas phase does anything to it, so a coupled document that runs the aerosol owns this state -- which is also why the gas mechanism must not own it (CLAUDE.md: a component does not own state a consumer will also drive). Default = the surface-noon state of the reference column."
        },
        "NH3": {
          "units": "molec/cm^3",
          "constant": true,
          "default": 14056082.525449336,
          "description": "NH3 (KPP VAR index 3), a RESERVOIR species of this mechanism. It is a KPP VAR species, but its only appearance in cbmz_mosaic.eqn is the identity row {125:105} NH3 = NH3, which has zero net stoichiometry and which KPP eliminates from Fun along with the reaction; the generated code writes Vdot = 0 for it and this document says the same thing with constant: true. NH3 is in the mechanism because MOSAIC partitions it into the aerosol, not because the gas phase does anything to it, so a coupled document that runs the aerosol owns this state -- which is also why the gas mechanism must not own it (CLAUDE.md: a component does not own state a consumer will also drive). Default = the surface-noon state of the reference column."
