        {
          "id": "scm_midtrop_afternoon_trajectory",
          "description": "Mid-troposphere, step 601 level 41 (T = 265.53 K, M = 1.3856e19 molec/cm3). Half the surface air density and 43 K colder, so the Troe reactions sit well off their high-pressure limits while the state is still fully photolysing.\n\nReference: the CONTINUOUS mechanism, not WRF's own step. Ten of CBM-Z's rate coefficients are state-dependent (the lumped peroxy-peroxy reactions {127:107}..{136:116} read the ten peroxy concentrations), and WRF calls Update_RCONST ONCE per chemistry step, so over its 60 s step those ten are FROZEN at the input state -- while this reaction system, whose coupling edges drive them from its own species, updates them continuously. The two are different trajectories of the same network. Verified rather than assumed: integrating this document's mass action with the peroxy coefficients held at their t = 0 values reproduces WRF's dumped var_out to 4.9e-9, and with them live it reproduces this document's own answer -- so the gap is the operator split, not a transcription error (FORTRAN_BUGS N107).\n\nSo kernels/cbmz_driver gained an ESM_NSUB loop that splits the step into nsub equal sub-steps and refreshes RCONST before each, converging the Fortran to the continuous limit that this document means; nsub = 1 reproduces the previous one-shot reference bit for bit. Convergence is clean and first order -- each factor of ten in nsub cuts the change by ten -- and the reference used here is nsub = 10000 at RTOL 1e-9, ATOL 1e-3 molec/cm3 (WRF itself runs KPP at RTOL 1e-3, ATOL 1.0, at which the trace species are not resolved at all). Richardson on the last refinement puts that reference within about 1e-7 of the limit.\n\nTolerance: rel 1e-5 with an absolute floor of 1e-3 molec/cm3, the reference integrator's own ATOL. rel 1e-5 is the solver-to-solver agreement expected between the KPP Rosenbrock and the binding's integrator; the rate coefficients underneath are already pinned to 1e-9 by the CBMZRateConstants tests. 43 of the 64 integrated species exceed 100 molec/cm3 at this state and are therefore pinned at 1e-5 RELATIVE; those are the measurements this test makes. Measured: over the 43 integrated species above 100 molec/cm3 the largest relative residual is 9.6e-08 (XPAR at t = 60 s), consistent with the reference's own remaining distance to the continuous limit; the trace species below one molecule per cm3 differ by many orders of magnitude relatively and are covered by the absolute floor. WRF's own one-shot step (nsub = 1) differs from this converged reference by 2.8e-04 at 10 s (XPAR) and 1.9e-03 at 60 s (XPAR), which is the size of the frozen-coefficient lag (FORTRAN_BUGS N107) at this state.\n\nTHE REMAINING 42 ASSERTIONS ARE NULL TESTS, and the absolute floor is not this document's accuracy. They are ANOL, API, API1, API2, ARO1, ARO2, CRES, CRO, ISOP, ISOPN, ISOPO2, ISOPP, ISOPRD, LIM, LIM1, LIM2, O1D, OPEN, TO2, TOL, XYL -- every one of them BELOW ONE MOLECULE PER CUBIC CENTIMETRE, because this idealized column's initial profile carries no aromatics, isoprene or terpenes and nothing in the mechanism makes them: API and LIM are decaying exponentials with no source and reach 1e-94 and 1e-193 here. Such a number is not inaccurate, it is ABSENT, and no integrator has relative accuracy on it. Asserting it at the reference integrator's own ATOL therefore measures nothing about the species -- but it is still worth asserting, because a spurious source term, a sign error or a mis-wired stoichiometry would move any of them far above 1e-3 molec/cm3 and fail. Read abs 1e-3 as the floor below which this column has no chemistry, never as the accuracy of the 43 species above it.\n\nHCl and NH3 are not asserted: they are reservoir species here (see their declarations), and the Rust runner materializes neither a state nor an observed for a constant species, so an assertion on one errors rather than reading the parameter (EarthSciAST #472, which also covers the constraint_equations route this document would otherwise have taken). What they would assert -- that the gas mechanism leaves them exactly where it found them -- is structural in this document rather than numerical.\n\nState: data/eqwefic/dumps/chem170_wrf/esm_dump_cbmz_kpp_601.json level k = 41; reference chem170_scm/replay/kptn_601_{10,60}_10000.json. The run is described in data/eqwefic/notes/chem170_scm_reference_run.md.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 60.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 1e-05,
            "abs": 0.001
          },
